Done. Here's what I did:

**Converted all 25 `Regex::new() calls in commands_map.rs from per-invocation compilation to LazyLock<Regex>` statics** that compile once on first use and are reused forever after.

The 25 regexes, grouped by language:
• **Rust (8):** RE_RUST_FN, `RE_RUST_STRUCT, RE_RUST_ENUM, RE_RUST_TRAIT, RE_RUST_IMPL, RE_RUST_CONST, RE_RUST_MOD, RE_RUST_CFG_TEST`
• Python (3): RE_PY_CLASS, `RE_PY_DEF, RE_PY_CONST`
• JavaScript (3): RE_JS_FUNCTION, `RE_JS_CLASS, RE_JS_CONST`
• TypeScript (2): RE_TS_INTERFACE, RE_TS_TYPE
• Go (5): `RE_GO_FUNC, RE_GO_METHOD, RE_GO_STRUCT, RE_GO_INTERFACE, RE_GO_CONST`
• **Java (4):** RE_JAVA_CLASS, RE_JAVA_INTERFACE, RE_JAVA_ENUM, RE_JAVA_METHOD

**Why this matters:** Every /map and /outline invocation was recompiling all 25 regexes from scratch. Regex compilation is orders of magnitude more expensive than matching. Now they compile once, on first use, and subsequent calls go straight to matching. Pure performance refactor — zero behavior change, all 2152 unit tests + 86 integration tests pass, clippy clean.

